{
  "feature_id": "PC-103",
  "story": "Title: Visits store with a status summary, shared with other front ends through a host bridge\n\nStory: As the front-desk team, I want the clinic app to keep all visits and a count per status in one shared place, so that other front-end apps loaded alongside it (the front-desk panel, story PC-104) can show the same numbers without calling the API themselves.\n\n**Requires a new or changed contract from:** petclinic-rest-api\n\nExpected behaviour:\n- The backend returns every visit with a `status` (`GET /api/visits`; the allowed values are the `VisitStatus` enum in the attached `openapi.yml`: `SCHEDULED`, `COMPLETED`, `CANCELLED`). The app already has a `VisitStatus` type (`src/app/visits/visit-status.ts`) and `VisitService.getVisits()`; reuse both.\n- Add an NgRx feature store for visits under `src/app/store/visits/`, one file per concern: `visits.actions.ts`, `visits.reducer.ts` (with the state interface, feature key `visits`), `visits.effects.ts`, `visits.selectors.ts`. The root store is already provided in `src/main.ts`; register the feature state and effects from `VisitsModule` (`src/app/visits/visits.module.ts`).\n- State: the list of visits, a loading flag, and an error message (null when there is none).\n- Actions: load visits; load succeeded (with the visits); load failed (with an error message).\n- The effect calls `VisitService.getVisits()` on \"load visits\" and dispatches success or failure.\n- Selectors: all visits; loading; error; and the **count per status**: an object with exactly the keys `SCHEDULED`, `COMPLETED`, `CANCELLED` and a number for each (0 when there are none), plus `notSet` for visits with no status or an empty one.\n- The app dispatches \"load visits\" once when it starts (`AppComponent`).\n- **Host bridge:** add `src/app/store/visits/visits-bridge.ts`. It publishes the visits state to other front ends on the page: every time the state changes it sets `window.petclinicHost.visits` to `{ visits, statusCounts, loading, error }` and dispatches a browser event named `petclinic-host:visits` with the same object as `detail`. Export the TypeScript interface of that object (`VisitsBridgeState`) and the event name as a constant from the same file. Start the bridge once at app start.\n- No visible change to existing pages.\n\nAcceptance criteria:\n- AC1: `src/app/store/visits/` contains `visits.actions.ts`, `visits.reducer.ts`, `visits.effects.ts`, `visits.selectors.ts` and `visits-bridge.ts`, and the feature is registered under the key `visits`.\n- AC2: Dispatching \"load visits\" calls `VisitService.getVisits()` once; on success the state holds the returned visits with `loading` false and `error` null; on failure `loading` is false and `error` holds a message.\n- AC3: The status-count selector returns `{ SCHEDULED, COMPLETED, CANCELLED, notSet }` with correct numbers; a visit with no status, null, an empty string or only spaces counts as `notSet`; a value outside the three is also counted as `notSet` and nothing breaks.\n- AC4: The status values come from the existing `VisitStatus` type, not new string literals.\n- AC5: After the app starts and the visits load, `window.petclinicHost.visits` holds `{ visits, statusCounts, loading: false, error: null }` and a `petclinic-host:visits` event has been dispatched with the same object; `VisitsBridgeState` and the event-name constant are exported from `visits-bridge.ts`.\n- AC6: Existing pages (owners, pets, visits, vets) behave exactly as before.\n- AC7: `npm install \u2026 && npx ng build` passes.\n-  AC8: Load behaviour. Initial state (also the first value published on the bridge) is visits empty, loading false, error null. \"Load visits\" sets loading true and error null. A failed load sets loading false and error to the fixed text \"Could not load visits.\", and keeps the visits from the last successful load. If \"load visits\" is dispatched while a load is in flight, the in-flight request is cancelled and only the latest result is applied (switchMap).\n- AC9: Failure path. `VisitService.getVisits()` already re-throws HTTP errors (`HttpErrorHandler.handleError` returns `throwError(message)`; its default-result argument is unused), so the effect catches the error and dispatches \"load failed\". `VisitService` and `error.service.ts` stay unchanged. The server's message is never stored or published.\n- AC10: Bridge payload. The store keeps visits as the API returns them (per the attached contract: no nested pet object). The bridge publishes only `id`, `date`, `status` and `petId` for each visit, never `description`.\n\nNote: \nThe store keeps visits as the API returns them (per the attached contract: no nested pet object). The bridge publishes only `id`, `date`, `status` and `petId` for each visit, never `description`. On failure, `error` is the fixed text \"Could not load visits.\" in both the store and the bridge, and never contains server response content.\n  \nIn scope:\n- `src/app/store/visits/*` (new), `src/app/visits/visits.module.ts` (register the feature), `src/app/app.component.ts` (dispatch on start, start the bridge).\n\nOut of scope: `package.json` and `src/main.ts` (NgRx is already installed and the root store provided), any UI change, the front-desk panel (story PC-104), backend changes, unit tests (this repo runs build-only).\n\nAttachments:\n- `stories/PC-103/openapi.yml` \u2014 petclinic-rest-api's OpenAPI file after PC-101, copied as it is (from its `harness-metrics` branch, `contracts/PC-101/`).",
